      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          How Does PDF Merging Work?
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          When you click Merge PDFs, the browser reads each selected file using the FileReader API and loads its bytes into the pdf-lib PDF parser. The tool then creates a new, empty PDF document and copies the pages from each source PDF into it in the order shown in your file list. Once all pages have been added, the combined document is serialized to a byte array and made available as a downloadable file using a Blob URL.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Pages are copied as PDF page objects, not rasterized to images. This means the text remains selectable, the vector graphics remain sharp, and embedded images retain their original quality in the output document.
        </p>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/60 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 space-y-1 overflow-x-auto">
